To compile on standalone PC:

Install libdyplo, e.g. build with
  git clone git://github.com/topic-embedded-products/libdyplo
  cd libdyplo
  autoreconf --install
  ./configure --prefix=$HOME/usr
  make -j 8
  make install

Set PKG_CONFIG_PATH to find it
  export PKG_CONFIG_PATH=$HOME/usr/lib/pkgconfig

Just open in Qt Creator and build.
  qtcreator pr-demo-gui.pro

On recent Ubuntu versions, qtcreator doesn't install the Qt5 kit, to get it
into your system use:
  sudo apt install qt5-doc qt5-doc-html qtbase5-doc-html qtbase5-dev qt5-qmake
After that, in "manage kits" add `/usr/lib/qt5/bin/qmake`.

To cross-compile and debug directly on target, see:
  http://downloads.topic.nl/dev.html
